[35.688, "o", "  \"lab1_prediabetes_eat\": {\r\n"]
[35.688, "o", "    \"answer\": \"I'm not a doctor, and a high glucose screening result does not by itself confirm pre-diabetes. For meals, use the quarter-quarter-half plate: 1/2 vegetables and fruit, 1/4 wholegrains or staples such as brown rice or oats, and 1/4 protein such as fish, chicken, tofu, eggs or beans. Keep carbohydrate portions sensible and spread them across regular meals. Choose water, kopi kosong or teh siew dai instead of sugary drinks. At the hawker centre, try economy rice with brown rice, two vegetables, one protein and less gravy. Avoid crash diets and skipping meals. Please arrange a doctor follow-up to understand the result and whether further checks are needed. \",\r\n"]
[35.703, "o", "    \"intent\": \"nutrition\",\r\n"]
[35.703, "o", "    \"risk_level\": \"moderate\",\r\n"]
